---

Most of the bundled instrument sounds in src/soundfonts/ come from the MIDI.js
soundfont collection (https://github.com/gleitz/midi-js-soundfonts), generated
from FluidR3_GM and MusyngKite, and are distributed under the MIT Licence.

---

The three pipe organ instruments are different, and carry a different licence.

  src/soundfonts/pipe_organ-mp3.js
  src/soundfonts/pipe_organ_full-mp3.js
  src/soundfonts/pipe_organ_flute-mp3.js

These are adaptations of the Bureå Church organ sample set, a recording of the
1967 Hammarberg organ in Bureå, Sweden, made in May 2010 by Lars Palo and
prepared for GrandOrgue by Lars Palo and Graham Goode.

    http://familjenpalo.se/vpo/about-burea-church/

The sample set is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.5
Sweden Licence:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5/se/deed.en

Those three files are adaptations of it, made by tools/build_soundfont.py, and
so are distributed under the same Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.5
Sweden Licence rather than under the MIT Licence above. Attribution is to Lars
Palo and Graham Goode. Anyone redistributing them, modified or not, must do so
under those same terms.

---

Three piano instruments come from FreePats (https://freepats.zenvoid.org/),
converted by tools/build_sf2.py from the soft velocity layers of each.

  src/soundfonts/soft_grand_piano-mp3.js
      From the Salamander Grand Piano, a Yamaha C5 recorded by Alexander Holm,
      in the SF2 edition assembled by Roberto (roberto@zenvoid.org) for
      FreePats. Creative Commons Attribution 3.0:
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

  src/soundfonts/yamaha_grand_piano-mp3.js
      From the YDP Grand Piano by Roberto for FreePats, built from the Zenph
      Studios Yamaha Disklavier Pro Piano Multisamples for OLPC, recorded by
      Dr. Mikhail Krishtal and his team at Zenph Studios. Creative Commons
      Attribution 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

  src/soundfonts/upright_piano-mp3.js
      From Upright Piano KW, a Kawai upright recorded by Gonzalo and Roberto
      for FreePats. Dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0:
      https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

---

One organ instrument is of unknown licence.

  src/soundfonts/magnificent_gothic-mp3.js

It is converted from Maggoth2.sf2, a 1995 Sound Blaster AWE32 soundfont that
records no author or copyright. Find out whether it may be redistributed before
it is included in anything given to anyone else.

---

The rest of this project, the converter included, remains MIT.
